file before I run it.

22
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:14,333
One tool call. Write, index.html, two
hundred and eighty-six lines, in one pass.

23
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,469
Then its own summary of what it built —

24
00:01:16,469 --> 00:01:21,126
and that summary is fluent, formatted, and
confident. It is also a claim. The file is

25
00:01:21,126 --> 00:01:25,070
the artifact. Whether the file does what I
asked is a separate question.

26
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:29,510
Claude says done. I check. The bang runs a
shell command from inside the session. Two

27
00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:33,745
hundred eighty-six lines. Local storage,
twice. Now the one I said out loud before

28
00:01:33,745 --> 00:01:37,774
I looked: no external requests — grep for
any URL or script tag. Nothing. That

29
00:01:37,774 --> 00:01:41,802
constraint held. Then the one I was
waiting for. Remove, and sort. Both there.

30
00:01:41,802 --> 00:01:43,610
One I was told about. One I wasn't.

31
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:47,745
So I tell it exactly what I found and
exactly what not to do. Take both out.

32
00:01:47,745 --> 00:01:51,829
Change nothing else. Don't touch the
styling. Three edits, one file. And the

33
00:01:51,829 --> 00:01:56,075
diff is all red — fourteen lines gone,
nothing added. That is the scope I asked

34
00:01:56,075 --> 00:01:58,010
for. Read the diff, not the summary.

35
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:02,189
Then — without being asked — it did one
more thing. It wrote a memory. Two files,

36
00:02:02,189 --> 00:02:06,164
outside my folder, in its own directory,
so it remembers next time that I want

37
00:02:06,164 --> 00:02:10,344
exactly what I asked for. It told me. I'd
have missed it if I'd stopped reading at

38
00:02:10,344 --> 00:02:14,523
'both removed.' That's the product working
as designed. It is also a decision made

39
00:02:14,523 --> 00:02:14,880
for me.

40
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:18,843
Check it. Git diff stat: one file,
fourteen deletions, nothing else in the

41
00:02:18,843 --> 00:02:23,021
tree. Grep for remove or sort: gone. Local
storage: still two. Inside the repo,

42
00:02:23,021 --> 00:02:26,829
'nothing else touched' is true. Then I
look where git can't. That memory

43
00:02:26,829 --> 00:02:29,790
directory. Two files. And the note it
wrote is about me.

44
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:33,599
Who did what. Step one was mine: the
sentence with five constraints in it —

45
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:37,710
that's problem formulation. Claude built
the file; the handoff condition was every

46
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:39,714
constraint holds under grep, and it did.

47
00:02:39,714 --> 00:02:43,925
Step three, the dangerous middle: reading
the plan and the file, and hearing 'delete

48
00:02:43,925 --> 00:02:47,684
option' and 'sorted' before running
anything. Claude removed both, cleanly.

49
00:02:47,684 --> 00:02:51,644
Then interpretive judgment: 'nothing else
touched' was true inside the tree and

50
00:02:51,644 --> 00:02:55,504
false outside it. Notice the zero. No
executive integration — one thread, one

51
00:02:55,504 --> 00:02:58,060
file. That's fine at this size. It won't
stay fine.

52
00:02:58,110 --> 00:03:02,290
So what was mine. I must decide what done
means — I wrote it down before it started.

53
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:06,321
I must read the file before I run it. And
I must look outside the folder, because

54
00:03:06,321 --> 00:03:10,451
the machine cannot tell me when it's done
something I'd mind; it sounded exactly as

55
00:03:10,451 --> 00:03:14,432
sure about the memory file as about the
form. Claude can write two hundred lines

56
00:03:14,432 --> 00:03:18,264
in one pass and remove exactly what I
name. Next time I keep the constraints.

57
00:03:18,264 --> 00:03:20,204
Six lines. Mine — and one of them says:

58
00:03:20,204 --> 00:03:21,100
don't remember me.

59
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:25,217
Let's recap with Claude. Vibecoding is
real: no code written by hand, a working

60
00:03:25,217 --> 00:03:28,976
tool in two turns. The first pass added
two features nobody asked for and

61
00:03:28,976 --> 00:03:33,249
